{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And Jacob came whole.</b> It means that Jacob came from Paddan to the border of the land of Israel. But our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted that he came to Shechem, and שלם would then be an expression of wholeness, not a place-name. This is what they said: whole in his body, whole in his Torah, whole in his wealth. And Dinah went out from there, and there the entire incident befell her; and likewise they said, of blessed memory, 'at Shechem they afflicted Dinah.' And what it says, <b>and he purchased the parcel of the field</b> — because he did not wish to be a lodger, but wished to establish a holding in it. And he did not do so with intent, but it came about as a sign of the future, for that place his sons would inherit before they dispossessed the inhabitants of the land." "<b>And written.</b> The sage Rabbi Abraham wrote that what it says, 'and he purchased the parcel of the field,' comes to teach that there is great distinction to the land of Israel, and whoever has a portion in it is regarded as though he has a portion in the World to Come."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:29.916519385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}